y not just a plain linear ramp?\n\nBecause the data is **heavy-tailed** — a few countries emit thousands of megatonnes while most emit\nalmost nothing. On a linear scale, **195 of these 198 countries fall into the bottom fifth of the\nrange**, so a continuous ramp paints nearly the whole world one pale tone and spends its colour on\ntwo or three outliers:\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ncanvasXpress(\n  data      = y,\n  smpAnnot  = x,\n  graphType = \"Map\",\n  colorBy   = \"CO2\",\n  topoJSON  = \"https://www.canvasxpress.org/data/maps/WORLD.json\",\n  mapId     = \"co2Linear\",\n  legendPosition = \"left\",\n  theme = \"solarized\",\n  title    = \"The same data on a plain linear ramp\",\n  subtitle = \"195 of 198 countries sit in the bottom fifth of the scale - the map goes flat\",\n  width  = 700,\n  height = 480\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-87196521e49fb3a0b9fd\" style=\"width:100%;height:445px;\" class=\"canvasXpress html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-87196521e49fb3a0b9fd\">{\"x\":{\"data\":{\"y\":{\"vars\":[\"CO2\"],\"smps\":[\"Afghanistan\",\"Albania\",\"Algeria\",\"Andorra\",\"Angola\",\"Anguilla\",\"Antigua & Barbuda\",\"Argentina\",\"Armenia\",\"Aruba\",\"Australia\",\"Austria\",\"Azerbaijan\",\"Bahamas\",\"Bahrain\",\"Bangladesh\",\"Barbados\",\"Belarus\",\"Belgium\",\"Belize\",\"Benin\",\"Bermuda\",\"Bhutan\",\"Bolivia\",\"Bosnia and Herzegovina\",\"Botswana\",\"Brazil\",\"British Virgin Islands\",\"Brunei Darussalam\",\"Bulgaria\",\"Burkina Faso\",\"Burundi\",\"Cambodia\",\"Cameroon\",\"Canada\",\"Cape Verde\",\"Central African Republic\",\"Chad\",\"Chile\",\"China\",\"Colombia\",\"Comoros\",\"Congo\",\"Cook Islands\",\"Costa Rica\",\"Croatia\",\"Cuba\",\"Cyprus\",\"Czechia\",\"Democratic Republic of the Congo\",\"Denmark\",\"Djibouti\",\"Dominican Republic\",\"Ecuador\",\"Egypt\",\"El Salvador\",\"Equatorial Guinea\",\"Eritrea\",\"Estonia\",\"Ethiopia\",